    "title": "Extend, turn base, go around",
    "shortExplanation": "Tower may stretch or shorten your circuit; a go-around is flown at once and answered briefly.",
    "overview": [
      "Extend downwind: keep flying downwind until Tower calls your base. Turn base now: turn at once.",
      "Go around: fly the go-around first, then acknowledge briefly. Workload is high, so every transmission is kept to a minimum."
    ],
    "whyItMatters": "These instructions resolve conflicts in the circuit; a late reaction removes the margin.",
